  "full_text": "Entertain God and your ass will follow. Hey, we got a package. Hey, that's my drums. I think that's my drums. No, no, no, it's not enough. I got like, I got more drums. Because like I broke a drum. But they're the same tone, you know, so it kind of is not, oh well. There's the neighbor. So, God said I'm mighty. Terry, the mighty above the 30. Might be above the 30. Mr. God. So, Mr. God is my only friend. King David. Fuck yeah. So, what do you want to do, Mr. God? It's a sunny day. There's a bird. Let's fucking kill that bird. Fucking fat person. Kill that bird. Get me. Yeah. Oh, at your house, you mean, or what? Oh, yeah, yeah. Yeah. Oh, this place. Yeah, huh? Yeah. Yeah, they've been busy, huh? Yeah. Is it the same owner? Oh, okay. Oh. Hold on to God's hand. Seek the Lord in his strength. Seek his face continually. Discovering and embracing God's will leads to some major adjustments. And it requires us to release and risk. Releasing the familiar and risking whatever future may bring. And the bottom line of fleshing out God's will... We are only finite human beings. We can only see the present and the past. The future is a little frightening to us. So we need to hold God's hand and trust him to calm our fears. And at those times when we're stubborn and resisting and God shakes us by the shoulders to get our attention, we're reminded that we don't call our own shots, that God has a plan for us, mysterious though it may seem, and we want to be in the center of it. And all the risks notwithstanding, that's still the safest place on earth to be.",
